  "id": "Compound::DB00145 - Gene::211",
  "verbalization": "Glycine appears to interact with Alas2 through binding, which is then linked to participation in multiple metabolic activities, including 5-aminolevulinate synthase activity, N-succinyltransferase activity, and succinyltransferase activity. These activities are all associated with Alas1, suggesting a potential pathway where Glycine influences Alas1 through its interaction with Alas2. The evidence indicates that Glycine may modulate Alas1 via a shared intermediate, Alas2, by activating or inhibiting the metabolic processes it participates in. The consistent binding of Glycine to Alas2 across all three paths supports a functional link between Glycine and Alas1, likely through a mechanism involving the regulation of metabolic pathways. The overlapping roles of Alas2 in different activities suggest that Glycine may exert its effect on Alas1 through a common molecular mechanism, possibly by influencing the activity of these enzymes in a coordinated manner.",
